        <tr><td><code>concentric</code></td><td>a, b</td><td>centres coincide</td><td>2</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="algorithm" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Solving: Levenberg–Marquardt</h2>
    <p>The solver minimises the sum of squared residuals with Levenberg–Marquardt and a central-difference Jacobian. Each step solves the damped normal equations by Cholesky factorisation; a step that lowers the residual is accepted and the damping drops, a step that does not is rejected and the damping grows. Because every step is the smallest change that reduces the residuals, a dragged point drags the rest of the sketch the way it would on a drawing board.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Build the residual function of every constraint, and record which constraint owns each equation.</li>
      <li>Start with λ = 1e-3. Solve (JᵀJ + λ·max(1, diag)) Δx = −Jᵀr; if Cholesky fails, multiply λ by 10 and retry.</li>
      <li>Accept the step if the residual norm drops (λ = max(λ/5, 1e-12)); otherwise λ ×= 10.</li>
      <li>Stop when the residual is below <code>tolerance</code> (1e-9) or after <code>maxIterations</code> (200).</li>
      <li>Analyse the Jacobian at the solution: rank by Gaussian elimination with full pivoting (tolerance 1e-7), null-space basis, free unknowns (component above 1e-6).</li>
    </ol>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Constant</th><th>Value</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>maxIterations default</td><td>200</td><td>SolveOptions</td></tr>
        <tr><td>tolerance default</td><td>1e-9</td><td>SolveOptions</td></tr>
        <tr><td>initial damping λ</td><td>1e-3</td><td>solveSketch</td></tr>
        <tr><td>damping floor</td><td>1e-12</td><td>solveSketch</td></tr>
        <tr><td>solved if residual ≤</td><td>1e-6</td><td>status</td></tr>
        <tr><td>rank tolerance</td><td>1e-7</td><td>nullSpace</td></tr>
        <tr><td>free-unknown threshold</td><td>1e-6</td><td>free points</td></tr>
        <tr><td>conflict threshold (per equation)</td><td>1e-6</td><td>conflicts</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="status" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Status and diagnosis</h2>
    <p>After solving, degrees of freedom = unknowns − rank and redundant equations = equations − rank. The status follows from those two numbers and from whether the residual reached 1e-6.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Condition</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>fully-constrained</code></td><td>solved, dof 0, no redundancy</td><td>nothing</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>under-constrained</code></td><td>solved, dof &gt; 0</td><td>add dimensions for the ids in <code>free</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>over-constrained</code></td><td>solved, redundant &gt; 0</td><td>remove a duplicate constraint (harmless but noisy)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>conflicting</code></td><td>not solved, redundant &gt; 0</td><td>fix the constraint in <code>conflicts[0]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>failed</code></td><td>not solved, no redundancy</td><td>start nearer the intended shape or raise maxIterations</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>These results come from running the solver on a rectangle drawn slightly askew: a(0,0) b(38,2) c(41,27) d(−1,24), with a fixed at the origin and the four lines horizontal/vertical.</p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="Real results, one per added constraint">
{"// + length(l1) = 40\n{\u0022status\u0022:\u0022under-constrained\u0022,\u0022dof\u0022:1,\u0022free\u0022:[\u0022c\u0022,\u0022d\u0022],\u0022iterations\u0022:3,\u0022redundant\u0022:0}\n// + length(l2) = 25\n{\u0022status\u0022:\u0022fully-constrained\u0022,\u0022dof\u0022:0,\u0022iterations\u0022:3,\u0022residual\u0022:7.95e-12,\n \u0022points\u0022:[[\u0022a\u0022,0,0],[\u0022b\u0022,40,0],[\u0022c\u0022,40,25],[\u0022d\u0022,0,25]]}\n// + length(l3) = 40   (implied by the others)\n{\u0022status\u0022:\u0022over-constrained\u0022,\u0022dof\u0022:0,\u0022redundant\u0022:1}\n// + length(l3) = 30   named \u0022bad\u0022\n{\u0022status\u0022:\u0022conflicting\u0022,\u0022redundant\u0022:1,\n \u0022conflicts\u0022:[\u0022bad\u0022,\u0022vertical#2\u0022,\u0022length#5\u0022,\u0022vertical#4\u0022],\n \u0022message\u0022:\u0022The constraints cannot all hold; the worst miss is bad\u0022}"}
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Least change, not least surprise">
      <p>With height still free, moving c to (55, 31) and solving gave c = (40, 27.5) and d = (0, 27.5): the free height settled at the mean of the dragged c.y (31) and the old d.y (24), because Levenberg–Marquardt makes the smallest change that satisfies the constraints.</p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="api" class="doc-section">
    <h2>API</h2>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Signatures">
{"export const solveSketch: (sketch: Sketch, options?: SolveOptions) => SolveResult\nexport const sketchProfiles: (sketch: Sketch, tolerance?: number /* 0.01 */) =>\n  { readonly loops: Vec2[][]; readonly open: Vec2[][] }\nexport const polygonArea: (ring: ReadonlyArray<Vec2>) => number   // positive counter-clockwise\nexport class SketchError extends Error {}\n\nexport interface SolveResult {\n  sketch: Sketch; status: SolveStatus; dof: number; iterations: number\n  residual: number          // largest absolute residual left\n  free: string[]            // points and circles that can still move\n  conflicts: string[]       // worst first, only when not solved\n  redundant: number\n  message?: string\n}"}
    </DocCode>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Plate with a hole, end to end">
{"import { solveSketch, sketchProfiles, polygonArea } from \u0022@cadcamfun/core\u0022\n\nconst P = (id: string, x: number, y: number) => ({ id, kind: \u0022point\u0022 as const, x, y })\nconst L = (id: string, p1: string, p2: string) => ({ id, kind: \u0022line\u0022 as const, p1, p2 })\n\nconst result = solveSketch({\n  entities: [P(\u0022a\u0022, 0, 0), P(\u0022b\u0022, 38, 2), P(\u0022c\u0022, 41, 27), P(\u0022d\u0022, -1, 24),\n    L(\u0022l1\u0022, \u0022a\u0022, \u0022b\u0022), L(\u0022l2\u0022, \u0022b\u0022, \u0022c\u0022), L(\u0022l3\u0022, \u0022c\u0022, \u0022d\u0022), L(\u0022l4\u0022, \u0022d\u0022, \u0022a\u0022),\n    P(\u0022o\u0022, 20, 12), { id: \u0022h\u0022, kind: \u0022circle\u0022, center: \u0022o\u0022, radius: 4 }],\n  constraints: [\n    { type: \u0022fixed\u0022, point: \u0022a\u0022, x: 0, y: 0 },\n    { type: \u0022horizontal\u0022, line: \u0022l1\u0022 }, { type: \u0022vertical\u0022, line: \u0022l2\u0022 },\n    { type: \u0022horizontal\u0022, line: \u0022l3\u0022 }, { type: \u0022vertical\u0022, line: \u0022l4\u0022 },\n    { type: \u0022length\u0022, line: \u0022l1\u0022, value: 40 }, { type: \u0022length\u0022, line: \u0022l2\u0022, value: 25 },\n    { type: \u0022distanceX\u0022, a: \u0022a\u0022, b: \u0022o\u0022, value: 20 }, { type: \u0022distanceY\u0022, a: \u0022a\u0022, b: \u0022o\u0022, value: 12.5 },\n    { type: \u0022diameter\u0022, circle: \u0022h\u0022, value: 10 },\n  ],\n})\nresult.status                       // \u0022fully-constrained\u0022, dof 0\nconst { loops } = sketchProfiles(result.sketch)\nloops.map((l) => [l.length, polygonArea(l)])\n// [[50, 78.333], [4, 1000]]   circle: 50 points; rectangle: 4 points, area 1000"}
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="profiles" class="doc-section">
    <h2>From sketch to profiles</h2>
    <code>sketchProfiles</code> chains lines and arcs end to end through their shared point ids into closed loops, and returns every circle as a loop of its own. An arc becomes points spaced so the chord stays within <code>tolerance</code> of the true arc (n = ⌈sweep / (2·acos(1 − tol/r))⌉, at least 2); a full circle gets at least 8 points. A chain that does not close is returned in <code>open</code> instead of being dropped.
    <DocViewer3D title="Slot from two arcs and two lines" caption="A 30 mm slot of radius 8: two arcs and two lines sharing end points, solved and chained by sketchProfiles into one 66-point loop (area 680.739 mm² against the exact 681.062 mm²; the polygon is inscribed, so it is always slightly smaller)." solids={[{"kind":"extrude","profile":[[0,8],[-0.784,7.961],[-1.561,7.846],[-2.322,7.656],[-3.061,7.391],[-3.771,7.055],[-4.445,6.652],[-5.075,6.184],[-5.657,5.657],[-6.184,5.075],[-6.652,4.445],[-7.055,3.771],[-7.391,3.061],[-7.656,2.322],[-7.846,1.561],[-7.961,0.784],[-8,0],[-7.961,-0.784],[-7.846,-1.561],[-7.656,-2.322],[-7.391,-3.061],[-7.055,-3.771],[-6.652,-4.445],[-6.184,-5.075],[-5.657,-5.657],[-5.075,-6.184],[-4.445,-6.652],[-3.771,-7.055],[-3.061,-7.391],[-2.322,-7.656],[-1.561,-7.846],[-0.784,-7.961],[0,-8],[30,-8],[30.784,-7.961],[31.561,-7.846],[32.322,-7.656],[33.061,-7.391],[33.771,-7.055],[34.445,-6.652],[35.075,-6.184],[35.657,-5.657],[36.184,-5.075],[36.652,-4.445],[37.055,-3.771],[37.391,-3.061],[37.656,-2.322],[37.846,-1.561],[37.961,-0.784],[38,0],[37.961,0.784],[37.846,1.561],[37.656,2.322],[37.391,3.061],[37.055,3.771],[36.652,4.445],[36.184,5.075],[35.657,5.657],[35.075,6.184],[34.445,6.652],[33.771,7.055],[33.061,7.391],[32.322,7.656],[31.561,7.846],[30.784,7.961],[30,8]],"height":4,"color":"#c8a48a"}]} />
    <p>The slot above solved as <code>over-constrained</code> with dof 0 and 1 redundant equation: making <code>top</code> horizontal is implied once c1–a1 and c2–b1 are vertical and c1, c2 share a y. The solve still succeeds; the status only flags the duplicate.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>SketchError: Duplicate entity id</code></td><td>two entities share an id</td><td>ids are unique across points, lines, circles and arcs</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>SketchError: Unknown unknown</code></td><td>a constraint names a point or circle that is not there</td><td>check the ids in the constraint</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>conflicting</code> with a long conflicts list</td><td>one wrong dimension pulls several equations off zero</td><td>fix the first entry; the rest are usually collateral</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>failed</code></td><td>the start is far from any solution</td><td>draw closer to the intended shape; raise maxIterations</td></tr>
        <tr><td>profile missing from <code>loops</code></td><td>a chain does not close: it is in <code>open</code></td><td>make end points shared ids, or add a coincident constraint</td></tr>
        <tr><td>circle has too few points</td><td>tolerance too coarse for a small radius</td><td>pass a smaller tolerance to sketchProfiles</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

